{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1924","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Balanced Subsequences"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A sequence of brackets is called balanced if one can turn it into a valid math expression by adding characters "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"'+'"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"'1'"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". For example, sequences "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"'(())()', '()',"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"'(()(()))'"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" are balanced, while "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"')(', '(()',"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"'(()))('"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" are not."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A subsequence is a sequence that can be derived from the given sequence by deleting zero or more elements without changing the order of the remaining elements."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given three integers $$$n$$$, $$$m$$$ and $$$k$$$. Find the number of sequences consisting of $$$n$$$ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"'('"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" and $$$m$$$ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"')'"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", such that the longest balanced subsequence is of length $$$2 \\cdot k$$$. Since the answer can be large calculate it modulo $$$1\\,000\\,000\\,007$$$ ($$$10^9 + 7$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test contains multiple test cases. The first line contains the number of test cases $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 3 \\cdot 10^3$$$). Description of the test cases follows."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each test case contains three integers $$$n$$$, $$$m$$$ and $$$k$$$ ($$$1 \\le n, m, k \\le 2 \\cdot 10^3$$$)"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, print one integer — the answer to the problem."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n2 2 2\n3 2 3\n3 2 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2\n0\n4\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For the first test case "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"\"()()\", \"(())\""}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" are the $$$2$$$ sequences"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For the second test case no sequence is possible."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For the third test case "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"\")((()\", \")(()(\", \")()((\", \"())((\""}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" are the $$$4$$$ sequences."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"D","problemCode":"1924D","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1924/problem/D"}